data/
logs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
# Throwaway probes and one-off analysis scripts, which all live at the repo
# root. The leading slash is load-bearing: an unanchored `_*.py` also matches
# `__init__.py`, which silently kept gui_app/backends/__init__.py out of a
# commit and broke the package on a fresh clone. The negation below is a second
# line of defence, because that failure is invisible to `git add`.
/_*.py
!**/__init__.py
.venv/
probe_out/

# Internal engineering notebook: kept on this machine, not published.
# Its history stays in the repo; it simply stops receiving updates upstream.
docs/PERF_EXPERIMENTS.md

# Dev-only files kept locally but not shipped in the public product tree
# (untracked 2026-09-21; git history preserves them, so `git log -- <path>` and
# a checkout of an older commit still have them). The offline test suite still
# runs locally; CONTRIBUTING.md explains where it lives. probe_network.py,
# gui_app/probe_guard.py and configure_nic.ps1 stay TRACKED on purpose — the
# install guide points users to them.
/test_*.py
/probe_abuse.py
/probe_cpu_load.py
/probe_lag.py
/probe_mp.py
/probe_flir.py
/probe_seq.py
/tools/
/docs/make_screenshots.py
/docs/make_example_plots.py
/gui_app/mp_framesync.py
